---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How I Check Evidence"
  description="How Shiwakshi Rashmi evaluates sources, distinguishes evidence from interpretation, and labels research confidence."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="mb-12 border-b border-parchment-300 dark:border-darkSurface-750 pb-8">
      <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-forest-700 dark:text-forest-400 block mb-2">
        Methodological Standards
      </span>
      <h1 class="font-editorial-heading font-serif text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-50 mb-4">
        How I Check Evidence
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-300 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        This publication documents independent UX and market research inquiries. To ensure clarity and intellectual integrity, I follow specific checks before publishing any article.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Evidence Status Guide -->
    <section class="space-y-8 mb-16">
      <h2 class="font-editorial-heading font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100 mb-6">
        Article Status Classifications
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-300">
        Every article on this website carries a status label indicating its research depth and evidentiary scope. I never use colour alone to communicate status; each badge includes a distinct symbol, text label, and definition:
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <!-- Literature Exploration -->
        <div class="p-5 rounded border border-slateAccent-200 dark:border-slateAccent-800 bg-slateAccent-50/50 dark:bg-darkSurface-850 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-slateAccent-700 dark:text-slateAccent-300">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 6.253v13m0-13C10.832 5.477 9.246 5 7.5 5S4.168 5.477 3 6.253v13C4.168 18.477 5.754 18 7.5 18s3.332.477 4.5 1.253m0-13C13.168 5.477 14.754 5 16.5 5c1.747 0 3.332.477 4.5 1.253v13C19.832 18.477 18.247 18 16.5 18c-1.746 0-3.332.477-4.5 1.253" />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider">Literature Exploration</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-400 leading-relaxed">
            Surveys published secondary research, peer-reviewed papers, and sociological frameworks to map what is already established about a human question.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Research in Progress -->
        <div class="p-5 rounded border border-forest-200 dark:border-forest-800 bg-forest-50/50 dark:bg-darkSurface-850 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-forest-700 dark:text-forest-300">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5H7a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2h-2M9 5a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2M9 5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2" />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider">Research in Progress</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-400 leading-relaxed">
            Documents active investigations, qualitative fieldwork frameworks, or conceptual interaction models that are undergoing iterative testing and reflection.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Critical Review -->
        <div class="p-5 rounded border border-parchment-300 dark:border-darkSurface-700 bg-parchment-150/60 dark:bg-darkSurface-850 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-ink-800 dark:text-ink-200">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3 6l3 1m0 0l-3 9a5.002 5.002 0 006.001 0M6 7l3 9M6 7l6-2m6 2l3-1m-3 1l-3 9a5.002 5.002 0 006.001 0M18 7l3 9m-3-9l-6-2m0-2v2m0 16V5m0 16H9m3 0h3" />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider">Critical Review</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-400 leading-relaxed">
            Evaluates existing tools, software paradigms, or research methodologies against empirical evidence, identifying where current conventions fall short.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- My Evidence Checks -->
    <div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-8">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-editorial-heading font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100">
          The Checks I Conduct Before Publishing
        </h2>
        <p>
          As an Insights Manager with over five years of consultancy research experience, I apply four rigorous checks to my writing:
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <strong>Primary Source Verification:</strong> Every citation is traced back to its original published source, verified DOI link, or archival publication. I do not cite secondary summaries or AI-generated abstracts without examining the source material.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Explicit Separation of Claims:</strong> I strictly separate what the empirical literature demonstrates from my own interpretive reflections as a UX practitioner. Where evidence is inconclusive or contested, I explicitly label it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Methodological Boundary Declaration:</strong> I state the limitations of every qualitative observation, sample size, or framework. I do not generalize small qualitative cohorts to population-wide truths.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Non-Clinical Scope Discipline:</strong> In writing on chronic and fluctuating conditions, I evaluate user experience, interface burden, and human behaviour outside clinic walls. I never make medical, diagnostic, or clinical claims.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="p-6 rounded bg-parchment-150 dark:bg-darkSurface-850 border-l-4 border-forest-700 dark:border-forest-500">
        <h3 class="font-serif font-semibold text-lg text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-50 mb-2">
          Independent Publication Note
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-300 mb-0">
          Articles on this website are written and edited independently. They reflect my professional practice, literature synthesis, and design reflections. They are not academic peer-reviewed journal papers or clinical trial reports.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
